{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_75050521f6d3:git:commit:1:2","created_at":"2026-09-22 18:23:18","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"system","role":"cli"}},"payload":{"step_name":"git:commit","phase":"1","iteration":2,"result_json":{"hash":"e25a295c7efff1688b6bb208e7492676328b1727","short_hash":"e25a295","message":"review: plan 209 phase 1 governance policy","files":["5x-cli/docs/development/reviews/run_75050521f6d3-phase-1-review.md","docs/development/runs/209-plan-review-governance-plan/run_75050521f6d3/steps.jsonl"]},"head_commit":"e25a295c7efff1688b6bb208e7492676328b1727","patch_id":"21e3ab022d3edb2e45fd8e23cfde03189442d588","diff_summary":{"files_changed":2,"insertions":123,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":null,"tokens_in":null,"tokens_out":null,"cost_usd":null,"model":null}}
{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_75050521f6d3:reviewer:commit:1:0","created_at":"2026-09-22 18:23:46","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"agent","role":"reviewer","provider":"claude-code"}},"payload":{"step_name":"reviewer:commit","phase":"1","iteration":0,"result_json":{"readiness":"not_ready","summary":"Phase 1 delivers pure, well-factored governance types, a fingerprint, and a closure/debt validator; tests, typecheck, and lint pass and the dependency boundary is clean. Three P1 policy defects reject legitimate verdicts in enforced mode: a fingerprint change on partially addressed findings, adjacent human_required debt with a credit claim, and debt-eligibility drift from plan 208. New closure blockers also skip the identity-field checks. Two items need human policy decisions before Phase 3/4 consume the validator.","items":[{"id":"P1.1","title":"A changed fingerprint on a remaining prior finding is rejected, which conflicts with partially_addressed","action":"human_required","reason":"closure.ts:509-522 emits PRIOR_FINDING_FINGERPRINT_CHANGED whenever the title, failure, or lowestCostCorrection of a still-open or partially-addressed item differs from the persisted identity, and enforced mode rejects the verdict. A partially addressed finding naturally narrows its remaining correction (probe confirmed). The plan treats a changed fingerprint as changed evidence, not as a rejection. Someone must choose: make it informational (severity or record the new fingerprint), or keep identity fields stable via a separate remaining-work field. This affects the Phase 3 protocol and Phase 7 templates.","priority":"P1"},{"id":"P1.2","title":"Adjacent human_required debt items with a creditClaim are rejected via DEBT_COUPLING_INELIGIBLE","action":"auto_fix","reason":"The plan permits adjacent debt in items[] with action human_required (no credit). validateDebtPolicy also runs assessDebtEligibility, which returns non_intrinsic and emits DEBT_COUPLING_INELIGIBLE, so enforced mode rejects the verdict (probe confirmed). Only the single adjacent/unrelated rule should produce coupling violations; non-intrinsic eligibility should mean zero credit. Add a test that adjacent + human_required + claim is valid.","priority":"P1"},{"id":"P1.3","title":"Debt eligibility recomputes plan-208 rules and diverges from eligibleN","action":"human_required","reason":"The plan says to reuse advisory evidence and not recalculate eligibility. assessDebtEligibility requires the reviewer to self-assess its own reviewer-authored claim, which plan-208 eligibleN does not require. Its not_simpler rule compares architectureDelta with minimalAlternativeArchitectureDelta instead of plan 208 architectureDelta<0. It rejects every ineligible claim instead of withholding credit. It adds an undocumented /^phase/ targetPhase format. Probes showed plan-208-credited claims rejected in both directions. Someone must decide which source of truth governs reviewer-authored claims and whether ineligibility rejects or only withholds credit.","priority":"P1"},{"id":"P1.4","title":"New closure-round blockers are not required to carry failure, lowestCostCorrection, or deltas, so they cannot be fingerprinted","action":"auto_fix","reason":"validateInitialItem runs only for initial reviews. A closure critical-safety, introduced, or re-raise item without failure or lowestCostCorrection validates (probe: valid true), but fingerprintItem returns null, so Phase 2 cannot persist its FindingIdentity or match deferrals. Apply the validateInitialItem field and material-failure checks to every new closure item not in requiredIds, and add tests.","priority":"P1"},{"id":"P2.1","title":"Critical-safety evidence regex also matches the failure text","action":"auto_fix","reason":"closure.ts:259-264 tests failure + lateDiscoveryEvidence together, so a safety keyword in failure satisfies the concrete-evidence requirement even when lateDiscoveryEvidence is contentless. Test lateDiscoveryEvidence alone.","priority":"P2"},{"id":"P2.2","title":"Add tests for untested diagnostic codes and stale-decision variants","action":"auto_fix","reason":"No tests cover PRIOR_FINDING_FINGERPRINT_CHANGED, PRIOR_FINDING_ITEM_MISSING/UNEXPECTED, INTRODUCED_AND_CRITICAL_CONFLICT, INTRODUCED_HUNK_EVIDENCE_INCOMPLETE, CRITICAL_SAFETY_SCOPE_INVALID, or PRIOR_DECISION_NEW_EVIDENCE_REQUIRED, and none cover superseded, inactive, or non-risk decisions. The debt tests use order-dependent [0] assertions. Follow the existing fixture pattern.","priority":"P2"},{"id":"P2.3","title":"isRiskDecision accepts invented defer/accept_risk aliases","action":"auto_fix","reason":"The plan defines only defer_accept_risk as the risk choice. Restrict isRiskDecision to it, and type ReviewDecision.choice when Phase 2 adds the payload union.","priority":"P2"}]},"head_commit":"e25a295c7efff1688b6bb208e7492676328b1727","patch_id":null,"diff_summary":{"files_changed":0,"insertions":0,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":179272,"tokens_in":36,"tokens_out":19767,"cost_usd":1.1827554,"model":"claude-opus-5-5"}}
{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_75050521f6d3:human:gate:1:1","created_at":"2026-09-22 18:24:20","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"human","role":"operator"}},"payload":{"step_name":"human:gate","phase":"1","iteration":1,"result_json":{"choice":"continue","guidance":"Follow the approved plan literally: treat a same-ID fingerprint change as visible changed evidence rather than an automatic closure rejection; preserve stable-ID accounting. Reuse plan-208 debt evidence and eligibleN semantics, enforcing only plan-209 complete-evidence, intrinsic-coupling, valid-target, and genuinely-simpler-After guardrails. Address all reviewer items P1.1-P2.3 and add the requested tests."},"head_commit":"e25a295c7efff1688b6bb208e7492676328b1727","patch_id":null,"diff_summary":{"files_changed":0,"insertions":0,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":null,"tokens_in":null,"tokens_out":null,"cost_usd":null,"model":null}}
